# /diligence-memo

Generalizes an existing production skill, `/diligence-memo`. Pulls together whichever of the
configured `diligence.specialists` are actually available for this
{{vocabulary.entity}} into one prose memo for
the {{org.approverTitle|| "decision-maker"}}.

---

## Before anything

Load `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O4. Unit of reuse: the full set
of specialist outputs. Any upstream specialist output newer than this
memo's own last run is what makes a memo rerun genuinely new work; an
unchanged specialist set means nothing to rewrite.

## What this skill does

1. Reads every available specialist output under
   `diligence/[{{vocabulary.entity}}]/outputs/` — "available" means however
   many of `diligence.specialists` actually completed; a memo with seven of
   eight specialists' worth of input still produces a full memo, stating
   plainly which one is missing and why, never silently proceeding as if
   the missing one didn't exist and never refusing to produce a memo at
   all over one gap.
2. Synthesizes across specialists per `standards/WRITING-STANDARDS.md` Rule
   W15 (quote an upstream phrase once, never twice — this memo's job is
   synthesis, not assembly of upstream sentences) and Rule G10 (any
   restated finding preserves the upstream specialist's exact scope,
   direction, and tense — re-read that specialist's own field before
   writing the sentence, never restate from memory).
3. Ends with exactly one line, verbatim, drawn from
   `vocabulary.verdicts` — no other value, no hedge word appended, no
   verdict invented that isn't in that configured list. This is a
   **mechanical check, not a stylistic one**: before the memo is considered
   finished, verify in code that its final line is exactly one of the
   configured verdict strings. A memo that fails this check is not
   finished, regardless of how complete its prose looks.

## Vertical-specific analytical frameworks

A vertical overlay may extend this template with its own scorecard or
summary framework (see `templates/verticals/vc/` for VC/PE's fit scorecard
and re-rate thesis summary, deliberately kept out of
`standards/EVIDENCE-STANDARDS.md` because they're not universal — a real
estate or insurance vertical's memo doesn't need a re-rate thesis at all).
Any such extension is additive to this base template, never a replacement
for the verdict-line requirement above.

---

## Output format

Prose memo, `standards/WRITING-STANDARDS.md` throughout (particularly W16
if this memo has an executive-summary section). Save per
`standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O1 under
`diligence/[{{vocabulary.entity}}]/outputs/`; render to PDF per Rule O2;
make the Rule O3 delivery offer.
